## 3. Owner entity and OwnerRepository

### Owner entity
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`

Extends `Person` (which provides `firstName`/`lastName`). Telephone-relevant parts:
```java
@Column(name = "telephone")
@NotEmpty
@Digits(fraction = 0, integer = 10)
@Pattern(regexp = "^[0-9]{10}$", message = "Phone number must be exactly 10 digits")
private String telephone;

public String getTelephone() { return this.telephone; }
public void setTelephone(String telephone) { this.telephone = telephone; }
```
Other fields: `address` (`@NotEmpty`), `city` (`@NotEmpty`), `Set<Pet> pets`. So the entity itself enforces a 10-digit telephone via `@Pattern`/`@Digits`.

`Person` superclass: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Person.java` — `firstName`, `lastName` (both `@NotEmpty`) with getters/setters.

### OwnerRepository interface
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/OwnerRepository.java`

All methods:
- `Collection<Owner> findByLastName(String lastName) throws DataAccessException`
- `Page<Owner> findByLastName(String lastName, Pageable pageable) throws DataAccessException`
