There is NO `findByTelephone` or any uniqueness-query method.

## 4. Existing telephone normalization logic

The ONLY normalization logic in the codebase is in `ValidateNewOwner.service` (above):
```java
String normalized = request.getTelephone().replaceAll("\\D", "");
if (normalized.length() != 10) {
    throw new InvalidTelephoneException(normalized);
}
request.setTelephone(normalized);
```
It strips all non-digits and requires exactly 10 digits. The normalized value is written back onto the request DTO so downstream BuildOwner/SaveOwner persist it.

Searches for "normaliz"/"normalize" found matches only in `ValidateNewOwner`, `InvalidTelephoneException`, and `InvalidTelephoneExceptionHandler` (all shown). There is NO telephone-uniqueness / duplicate-detection logic anywhere in `src/main/java` (grep for conflict/duplicate/findByTelephone/unique found nothing relevant — only unrelated matches in `SpecialtyResolution` and `Role`).

