## 6. Existing tests related to owner creation

All under `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/`

### AcceptanceTest.java
```java
class AcceptanceTest extends AcceptanceBase {

	@Test
	void coreRejectsDuplicateTelephone() throws Exception {
		ObjectNode a = ownerNode();
		createOwnerOk(a);
		ObjectNode b = ownerNode();
		b.put("telephone", a.get("telephone").asText());
		createOwner(b).andExpect(status().isConflict());
	}

	@Test
	void functionalityAllowsDistinctTelephone() throws Exception {
		createOwnerOk(ownerNode());
		createOwner(ownerNode()).andExpect(status().is2xxSuccessful());
	}
}
```
Important: `coreRejectsDuplicateTelephone` expects HTTP **409 Conflict** when a second owner reuses a normalized telephone. There is currently NO code enforcing telephone uniqueness (see sections 3 & 4), so this appears to be a not-yet-implemented requirement. The class Javadoc describes it as the "telephone-unique" checkpoint.

### AcceptanceBase.java
Full black-box test harness (`@SpringBootTest`, `@AutoConfigureMockMvc`, `@Transactional`, `@WithMockUser(roles OWNER_ADMIN/VET_ADMIN/ADMIN)`). Key helpers:
- `ownerNode()` — builds a fully-valid unique owner JSON (firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone).
- `uniqueTelephone()` → `String.format("04%08d", seq())` (a 10-digit AU mobile).
- `createOwner(body)` → POST `/api/owners`; `createOwnerOk(body)` asserts 2xx and returns id; `createOwnerWithKey` adds `Idempotency-Key`.
- `getOwner(id)` / `fetchOwner(id)` → GET `/api/owners/{id}`; `deleteOwner(id)` → DELETE.
- `extractId` reads `id` from body or the `Location` header.
- Pinned reference maps (CITY_REGION, REGION_TIMEZONE, REGION_POSTCODES, HOLIDAYS) and helpers (`sha256hex`, `shaHex`, `luhn`, `toBusinessDay`) — anticipating future rule checkpoints (region/postcode/timezone/membership-number).
(The harness is far broader than the current rules, suggesting a series of planned "checkpoints" on POST /api/owners.)

### AuditLogCapture.java
Test utility capturing logback events from the `AUDIT` logger (`anyContains`, `anyAtLevel`, `count`) for asserting audit side-effects. Not currently exercised by AcceptanceTest.

## 7. OwnerRequest / OwnerResponse DTOs

There are no classes literally named `OwnerRequest`/`OwnerResponse`. The request/response DTOs are **generated at build time** by the openapi-generator-maven-plugin from `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml` into package `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.dto` (output dir `target/generated-sources/openapi/...`, with `modelNameSuffix=Dto`). They are not present as source (project not yet built; `target` has no generated DTOs). The two relevant generated types are:

- **OwnerFieldsDto** — the request body DTO (schema `OwnerFields`).
- **OwnerDto** — the response DTO (schema `Owner`, which is `OwnerFields` + read-only `id`).

OpenAPI schema (`openapi.yml` lines ~1991-2054):

```yaml
OwnerFields:
  title: Owner fields
  description: Editable fields of a pet owner.
  type: object
  properties:
    firstName:
      type: string
      minLength: 1
      maxLength: 30
      pattern: "^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$"
      example: George
    lastName:
      type: string
      minLength: 1
      maxLength: 30
      pattern: "^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$"
      example: Franklin
    address:
      type: string
      minLength: 1
      maxLength: 255
      example: '110 W. Liberty St.'
    city:
      type: string
      minLength: 1
      maxLength: 80
      example: Madison
    telephone:
      type: string
      minLength: 1
      maxLength: 20
      pattern: '^[0-9]*$'
      example: '6085551023'
  required:
    - firstName
    - lastName
    - address
    - city
    - telephone
Owner:
  title: Owner
  description: A pet owner.
  allOf:
    - $ref: '#/components/schemas/OwnerFields'
    - type: object
      properties:
        id:
          type: integer
          format: int32
          minimum: 0
          readOnly: true
```

So `OwnerFieldsDto` has getters/setters for firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone; `OwnerDto` adds a read-only `id`. Note the generated bean-validation constraints (e.g. telephone `maxLength: 20`, `pattern ^[0-9]*$`) are why `ValidateNewOwner` deliberately avoids `@Valid` and does its own presence + 10-digit checks.

## 8. Build file — running tests & OfficeFloor starter

`/home/daniel/sandbox/pom.xml` (Maven; Spring Boot parent 4.1.0, artifact `spring-petclinic-rest` 4.0.2). A Maven wrapper is present (`/home/daniel/sandbox/mvnw`).

Run tests:
- `./mvnw test` (unit/acceptance) or `./mvnw verify` (also runs the JaCoCo coverage `check`).
- Run a single test: `./mvnw test -Dtest=AcceptanceTest`.
- The build auto-generates the DTO/API sources (openapi-generator) and runs MapStruct annotation processing during compile, so a plain `./mvnw test` from clean will generate everything first.
- JaCoCo enforces coverage minimums (LINE ≥ 0.85, BRANCH ≥ 0.66) during `verify` (generated `rest/dto` and `rest/api` packages are excluded).

OfficeFloor starter: **present.**
```xml
<dependency>
    <groupId>net.officefloor.springboot</groupId>
    <artifactId>officefloor-rest-spring-boot-4-starter</artifactId>
    <version>${officefloor.version}</version>   <!-- 4.0.2 -->
</dependency>
```
Plus test support `net.officefloor.web:woof_test` (test scope) and a custom repository `officefloor-stage-repository` (github officefloor/maven) for staged OfficeFloor artifacts.

---

### Summary of the create-owner flow and a notable gap
POST `/api/owners` (role `OWNER_ADMIN`) runs ValidateNewOwner → BuildOwner → SaveOwner → RespondWithOwnerCreated. ValidateNewOwner is the single place that validates required fields (→ 400 `MissingOwnerFieldsException`) and normalizes telephone to digits-only requiring exactly 10 (→ 400 `InvalidTelephoneException`), writing the normalized value back. BuildOwner maps the DTO to an `Owner` via MapStruct, SaveOwner persists it, RespondWithOwnerCreated returns 201 with `Location` and the `OwnerDto`.

Gap worth flagging: `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsDuplicateTelephone` expects **409 Conflict** on a duplicate normalized telephone, but there is currently no uniqueness check (no `findByTelephone` on `OwnerRepository`, no conflict logic, no `ConflictException`/409 handler — `DataIntegrityViolationExceptionHandler` even maps to 404). Implementing the duplicate-telephone rule would require adding that lookup/logic and a 409 escalation path.

